    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{a}$, squashed, stretched.",
      "worked": "To keep the original input $u$, set $ax=u$, so the new horizontal coordinate is $x=\\frac{u}{a}$. The horizontal scale factor is $\\frac{1}{a}$. If $a>1$, then $\\frac{1}{a}<1$ and the graph is squashed. If $0<a<1$, then $\\frac{1}{a}>1$ and the graph is stretched.",
